<h1>California Sea Change Atlas</h1>
</div>
<p class="lede">The CA Sea Change Atlas (CASCA) is two tools for making sense of California's sea-level-rise and coastal-flooding visualisation tools: a side-by-side map collating publicly accessible data, and a side-by-side comparison of select tools.</p>
<p class="hero-about-link">This site is under active development; some things may break and some may not yet have been verified by a human. Inspired by "Sea the Future," a decision tool summarizing California sea level rise and flood visualization tools. <a href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">Read more</a></p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="main">
<div class="wrap">

<div class="landing-cards">
<div class="landing-card">
<img src="{{ '/img/preview-map.png' | url }}" alt="Screenshot of the CASCA map page" loading="lazy" onerror="this.remove()">
<h2>CASCA Map</h2>
<p>A Leaflet map with toggleable layers collated from the sea-level-rise and coastal-flooding mapping tools that have publicly accessible endpoints. Use this when you want to compare layers side-by-side and scenarios for a specific piece of California coastline. Not every resource appears here; see the comparison tool for the full list.</p>
<a class="landing-card-cta" href="{{ '/map/' | url }}">Open the map</a>
</div>
<div class="landing-card">
<img src="{{ '/img/preview-sources.png' | url }}" alt="Screenshot of the CASCA tool comparison page" loading="lazy" onerror="this.remove()">
<h2>CASCA Comparison Tool</h2>
<p>A filterable grid of sea-level-rise and coastal-flooding visualization resources California residents and planners might use, plus a compare-up-to-three table covering scope, process, exposure, data, and known limitations. Use this when you're deciding which tool can contribute to answering your question.</p>
<a class="landing-card-cta" href="{{ '/compare/' | url }}">Browse the resources</a>
</div>
</div>

</div>
</div>

<script>
// Size the logo to the home page heading's height so it matches the title text at any width.
(function () {
  var h1 = document.querySelector(".hero-title h1");
  var box = document.querySelector(".hero-title");
  if (!h1 || !box) return;
  function sync() { box.style.setProperty("--logo-size", h1.offsetHeight + "px"); }
  sync();
  if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(sync);
  if (window.ResizeObserver) new ResizeObserver(sync).observe(h1);
})();
</script>
